Description: copies of files clone their blocks where the file system can (FreeBSD: copy_file_range(2) with COPY_FILE_RANGE_CLONE, which ZFS does with block cloning), with an option to turn it off (file_cloning, "Use COW file cloning")
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/aee540f8d4b8503ffd2a3925d5fefc2f33d086a5
 (31.03.2026, after 4.8.33, by PR https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/pull/5083; no release has it), backported to the
 code of 4.8.33. With it the fixes of upstream for the indices of the widgets of the
 configuration dialog it moves (https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/0792bcee45a0659f8a319ccdfd6ee323b6d07ec8,
 https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/198ec936cedd643c34f23a1a3e6a6de63f99fc1b)
Bug: https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/issues/5082
Why: aZ (12.11.2026): our servers run FreeBSD 15.1 or later, whose OpenZFS (2.4.2) has
 block cloning on (vfs.zfs.bclone_enabled=1); the FreeBSD port of mc lacks this only
 because no release of mc has come since. configure.ac checks copy_file_range on FreeBSD
 (FICLONERANGE on Linux, clonefile on macOS, reflink on Solaris) and defines
 HAVE_FILE_CLONING_BY_RANGE; mc-build.sh runs autoreconf for it and checks the defines.
 copy_file_file() tries vfs_clone_file() first (not for an O_APPEND destination; for a
 Reget from the end of the destination) and copies as before when the clone fails (other
 file systems, another pool, cloning off). file_cloning (on by default) is in
 [Midnight-Commander] of ~/.config/mc/ini and in Options, Configuration, "Use COW file
 cloning". The unit test of upstream comes with it (tests/lib/vfs/vfs_clone_file.c).

